  "desc": "17 rockets lined up by height in 3D, from a 1.7 m person to Starship. Rockets from the US, Japan, Europe and India.\nHeights are official figures (\"about\" means the official figure is rounded). Widths, shapes and colors are simplified and approximate.\n\nChapters\n0:00 Intro\n0:04 Person\n0:15 Electron\n0:27 Epsilon (Japan)\n0:38 Mercury-Redstone (1961)\n0:50 Vega-C (Europe)\n1:01 LVM3 (India)\n1:13 PSLV (India)\n1:24 H-IIA (Japan)\n1:36 H-IIB (Japan)\n1:47 Vulcan\n1:59 H3 (Japan)\n2:10 Falcon 9\n2:22 Falcon Heavy\n2:33 New Glenn\n2:45 SLS (Artemis)\n2:56 Saturn V (Apollo)\n3:08 Starship\n3:19 All side by side\n\nHeight sources\n- Electron: Rocket Lab https://rocketlabcorp.com/assets/Uploads/RL-EducationGraphics-About-Rocket-Lab-and-Electron.pdf\n- Epsilon (Japan): JAXA https://fanfun.jaxa.jp/faq/detail/292.html\n- Mercury-Redstone (1961): NASA https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/marshall/mercury-redstone-launch-vehicle/\n- Vega-C (Europe): ESA https://www.esa.int/Enabling_Support/Space_Transportation/Vega/Vega-C\n- LVM3 (India): ISRO https://www.isro.gov.in/GSLVmk3_CON.html\n- PSLV (India): ISRO https://www.isro.gov.in/PSLV_CON.html\n- H-IIA (Japan): JAXA https://www.rocket.jaxa.jp/rocket/h2a/\n- H-IIB (Japan): JAXA https://fanfun.jaxa.jp/faq/detail/292.html\n- Vulcan: ULA https://www.ulalaunch.com/docs/default-source/rockets/vulcancentaur.pdf\n- H3 (Japan): JAXA https://www.jaxa.jp/projects/pr/brochure/pdf/01/rocket09.pdf\n- Falcon 9: SpaceX https://new.spacex.com/vehicles/falcon-9\n- Falcon Heavy: SpaceX https://new.spacex.com/vehicles/falcon-heavy\n- New Glenn: Blue Origin https://www.blueorigin.com/new-glenn\n- SLS (Artemis): NASA https://www.nasa.gov/reference/space-launch-system/\n- Saturn V (Apollo): NASA https://www.nasa.gov/learning-resources/for-kids-and-students/what-was-the-saturn-v-grades-5-8/\n- Starship: SpaceX https://new.spacex.com/vehicles/starship\n\nMusic: original\n\n#space #rocket #sizecomparison"
